			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Extend RPC route manifest with new Webview and Debug handlers\n\nUpdate the generated RouteManifest to include newly registered Mountain-side RPC methods, specifically adding Webview registration/unregistration, raw HTML/message passing, and Debug session controls. This increases the total count of known Mountain methods from 86 to 91.\n\nThe change ensures the Extension Host (Cocoon) correctly recognizes and routes these additional commands defined in the upstream VS Code workbench services to the Rust backend (Mountain). All corresponding build artifacts in the `Target/` directory have been regenerated to reflect the updated method map, ensuring consistency between the service routing logic and the compiled extension host bundle.",
			"SHA": "4f6581102a3e15ce2fc1cd07dcceec23b1f3623f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:41:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				797,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Standardize ESBuild configuration formatting and restore debuggability\n\nReformat ESBuild configuration files in `Configuration/ESBuild/` and `Source/ESBuild.js` to align with the project's strict formatting standards while maintaining the recently restored debuggability features. Apply consistent indentation, trailing commas, and line breaks across `BaseConfig`, `TargetConfig`, `CompileConfig`, and `Cocoon` entry points.\n\nRefactor `MountainConfig.js` to enforce consistent array and object formatting for validation logic, ensuring `loadMountainConfigFromEnv` and `validateMountainConfig` remain readable. Update `Cocoon.js` to explicitly re-export `EnvironmentConstant` and standardize the definition of `CocoonESBuildDevConfig` and `CocoonESBuildProdConfig` with proper comma placement.\n\nEnsure all source maps (`.js.map`) remain enabled for both configuration and target outputs, preserving full stack traces for production error triage as per the previous revert of aggressive minification. This change harmonizes the build pipeline's code style with the project's PascalCase naming conventions without altering functional behavior.",
			"SHA": "51690606fd03aa650d8d0bd8b29d47f2c7c0877f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:41:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",
				797,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Restore PascalCase naming and re-enable source maps for build system\n\nRevert the previous aggressive minification strategy for the Cocoon extension host to align with project naming standards and restore debuggability. Rename all exported ESBuild configuration constants and functions (e.g., `BaseConfig`, `CompileConfig`, `TargetConfig`, `CocoonESBuildConfig`) from single-character identifiers back to descriptive PascalCase names in `Configuration/ESBuild/`.\n\nRe-enable full source map generation (`.js.map`) for all configuration files and the entire `Target/` build output directory. This includes critical services such as `RPCServer`, `MountainClient`, `FileSystemRoute`, and `TypeConverter`, ensuring full stack traces are available for production error triage. Update `BaseConfig` to explicitly import environment constants (`On`, `Clean`, `Bundle`, `Compile`) from `Constant/EnvironmentConstant.js` for deterministic build behavior. Refactor `MountainConfig.js` to use named functions (`loadMountainConfigFromEnv`, `validateMountainConfig`, `createMountainConfig`, `getMountainConfigSummary`) with enhanced TLS and connection parameter validation.\n\nThis change ensures production artifacts remain maintainable and debuggable while enforcing consistent naming conventions across the build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "18645cd2cdc945ba7c38cc9d8dddf5be368b0493"
		},
